Model Sadia Khan mourned the death of her cousin, remembering her as more than family &mdash; an elder sister and a &ldquo;beautiful soul&rdquo; who held a special place in her heart.
Khan shared the news in an emotional post on Instagram, revealing that her cousin had been battling liver cancer and died after facing the illness with strength.
&ldquo;Today, I lost someone who was not just my cousin, but an elder sister and a beautiful soul who held such a special place in my heart,&rdquo; she wrote.
Remembering her cousin, Khan said she had spent years giving love, helping others and being there for the people around her. She also reflected on the strength her cousin had shown while battling cancer.
Khan revealed that she was on a plane when she learned of her cousin&rsquo;s death, making the moment even more difficult.
&ldquo;I am on a plane right now, and my heart feels so heavy. I feel helpless that I had to leave, but I pray Allah knows my heart, my intentions, and that I did everything I could for her,&rdquo; she wrote.
Among the memories Khan said she would carry with her were the final duas her cousin gave her while holding her hand.
&ldquo;The precious duas she gave me while holding my hand are something I will carry with me for the rest of my life. Those moments are everything to me,&rdquo; she shared.
