Alongside Quraishi and Farooq, the lead cast includes Shamoon Abbasi as the antagonist. The film was written by Abu Aleeha and produced by Farooq herself.
Quraishi plays a righteous police officer who is nicknamed &ldquo;Mango Jutt&rdquo; by Farooq&rsquo;s character, who tells him that he is both sweet and pretty. The film combines stunt-heavy action with comedic and romantic beats, embracing the larger-than-life sensibilities associated with the genre.
Mango Jutt marks Farooq&rsquo;s first big-screen appearance in five years, following 2019&rsquo;s Heer Maan Ja, as well as her first Punjabi-language film.
The project faced delays during development and post-production after filming wrapped. Its teaser surfaced in mid-2026, followed by Wednesday&rsquo;s trailer, but a release date has yet to be announced.
